ing Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of font names.The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font vs. a music font.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"color","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"halign","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In cases where text extends over more than one line, horizontal alignment and justify values can be different. The most typical case is for credits, such as:","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"valign","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The valign attribute is used to indicate vertical alignment to the top, middle, bottom, or baseline of the text. Defaults are implementation-dependent.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"smufl","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The smufl attribute group is used to indicate a particular Standard Music Font Layout (SMuFL) character. Sometimes this is a formatting choice, and sometimes this is a refinement of the semantic meaning of an element.","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlotherdirection\/init(id:value:printsobject:position:font:color:halign:valign:smufl:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Initializer","title":"init(id:value:printsObject:position:font:color:halign:valign:smufl:)","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLOtherDirectionV2id5value12printsObject8position4font5color6halign6valign5smuflACSSSg_SSSbSgAA11MXLPositionVAA7MXLFontVAA8MXLColorVSgAA18MXLLeftCenterRightOSgAA9MXLValignOSgAA17MXLSmuflGlyphNameVSgtcfc","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kin